{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest an itinerary most fine\nFor thy journey to Japan a land of rising sun's shine\nHerein lies a plan most wondrous to guide thee on thy way\n\nDay the First\nArrive in Tokyo's bustling streets where neon lights do play\nCheck into thy lodgings and take a moment to rest thy weary head\nThen venture forth to Shibuya Crossing where crowds do throng and sway\nVisit the famous statue of Hachiko the loyal canine friend\n\nDay the Second\nRise with the sun and visit the Meiji Shrine a sacred place of old\nDedicated to the deified spirits of Emperor Meiji and his wife\nNext make thy way to Harajuku where fashion's latest trends do unfold\nTake a stroll down Takeshita Street and marvel at the colorful sights to behold\n\nDay the Third\nTravel to Nikko a city nestled in the mountains' verdant fold\nVisit the Toshogu Shrine a UNESCO World Heritage Site of great renown\nMarvel at the ornate decorations and the resting place of Tokugawa Ieyasu\nThen return to Tokyo and enjoy a traditional Japanese dinner of sushi and sashimi\n\nDay the Fourth\nTake a bullet train to Kyoto a city steeped in history and tradition\nVisit the Kinkaku-ji Temple a golden pavilion of breathtaking beauty\nNext stroll through the serene gardens of the Fushimi Inari Shrine\nAnd watch the sunset over the city's rooftops a sight most divine\n\nDay the Fifth\nRise early and visit the Kiyomizu-dera Temple a UNESCO World Heritage Site\nPerched on a hill overlooking the city a place of great spiritual might\nThen explore the narrow streets of Gion where geisha and maiko do stroll\nAnd enjoy a traditional Japanese tea ceremony in a tranquil setting most serene\n\nDay the Sixth\nTravel to Nara a city of ancient temples and friendly deer\nVisit the Todai-ji Temple home to the largest bronze Buddha in the land\nNext explore the Nara Park where deer roam freely an